<title>CANADA: Loewen says shareholder suit without merit.</title>
<headline>Loewen says shareholder suit without merit.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Loewen Group Inc said on Tuesday that a shareholder class action lawsuit against it was without merit and that it expected to win the case.</p>
<p>Shareholder Jerry Krim filed the case in California Superior Court in Los Angeles last week seeking to force the funeral service company and its directors to negotiate with bidder Service Corp International.</p>
<p>Loewen &quot;believes the suit is without merit. It is regrettable that these kind of suits have become somewhat routine. The company intends to vigorously defend itself...and it expects to prevail,&quot; a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Vancouver Bureau (604) 664-7314</p>
</text>
